{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BH6PJ3JBgLXiSiGM96tYk1","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.4-uc001-md5sum\n     2→title: \"Compute and verify MD5 digests via md5sum\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go md5sum binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary\n     6→  computes MD5 digests and prints them in GNU format, or verifies a checksum file.\n     7→  The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n     8→  reference binary (gmd5sum from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that\n     9→  their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd030-md5sum.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/md5sum.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go md5sum binary on a file or stdin.\n    21→      Example: md5sum somefile.txt\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/md5sum reads each file, computes its MD5 digest using crypto/md5, and prints\n    25→      the result in GNU format to stdout.\n    26→  - id: F3\n    27→    step: |\n    28→      In check mode (--check), cmd/md5sum reads a checksum file, recomputes each digest,\n    29→      and prints OK or FAILED for each entry.\n    30→  - id: F4\n    31→    step: |\n    32→      The differential testing harness executes both ./bin/md5sum and gmd5sum with the\n    33→      same inputs and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n    34→  - id: F5\n    35→    step: |\n    36→      The harness verifies exit codes. If outputs and exit codes match, the test passes.\n    37→  - id: F6\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      If they diverge, the harness reports the triggering args, both outputs, and both\n    40→      exit codes.\n    41→\n    42→touchpoints:\n    43→  - T1: \"cmd/md5sum — digest computation, GNU format output, check mode, binary/tag flags (prd030-md5sum R1, R2, R3)\"\n    44→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    45→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    46→\n    47→success_criteria:\n    48→  - id: S1\n    49→    criterion: cmd/md5sum compiles and ./bin/md5sum exists after mage build.\n    50→  - id: S2\n    51→    criterion: The differential test for digest computation passes; output matches gmd5sum byte-for-byte.\n    52→  - id: S3\n    53→    criterion: The differential test for stdin (-) passes; output format matches gmd5sum.\n    54→  - id: S4\n    55→    criterion: The differential test for --check on a valid file passes; exits 0 and prints OK lines.\n    56→  - id: S5\n    57→    criterion: The differential test for --check on a file with a mismatch passes; exits 1 and prints FAILED.\n    58→  - id: S6\n    59→    criterion: The differential test for --tag passes; BSD format output matches gmd5sum --tag.\n    60→\n    61→out_of_scope:\n    62→  - HMAC-MD5 variants are not tested.\n    63→  - md5sum is not used for security; only format compatibility is verified.\n    64→\n    65→test_suite: test-rel05.4\n    66→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03d99544-4816-4711-bdea-ceb9935b9c36","uuid":"1b8b30ff-a4d9-4255-86f3-d4e5578418e8","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/367/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.4-uc001-md5sum.yaml","content":"id: rel05.4-uc001-md5sum\ntitle: \"Compute and verify MD5 digests via md5sum\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go md5sum binary on one or more files or stdin. The binary\n  computes MD5 digests and prints them in GNU format, or verifies a checksum file.\n  The differential testing harness then runs both the Go binary and the Homebrew\n  reference binary (gmd5sum from coreutils) with identical inputs and confirms that\n  their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd030-md5sum.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/md5sum.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go md5sum binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: md5sum somefile.txt\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/md5sum reads each file, computes its MD5 digest using crypto/md5, and prints\n      the result in GNU format to stdout.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      In check mode (--check), cmd/md5sum reads a checksum file, recomputes each digest,\n      and prints OK or FAILED for each entry.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness executes both ./bin/md5sum and gmd5sum with the\n      same inputs and compares stdout byte-for-byte.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness verifies exit codes. If outputs and exit codes match, the test passes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If they diverge, the harness reports the triggering args, both outputs, and both\n      exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/md5sum — digest computation, GNU format output, check mode, binary/tag flags (prd030-md5sum R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/md5sum compiles and ./bin/md5sum exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for digest computation passes; output matches gmd5sum byte-for-byte.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for stdin (-) passes; output format matches gmd5sum.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for --check on a valid file passes; exits 0 and prints OK lines.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for --check on a file with a mismatch passes; exits 1 and prints FAILED.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: The differential test for --tag passes; BSD format output matches gmd5sum --tag.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - HMAC-MD5 variants are not tested.\n  - md5sum is not used for security; only format compatibility is verified.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.4\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
